 "rules": {
  "frameworks": "NHS Supply Chain framework names matching /\\b(total orthopaedic solutions|surgical navigation)\\b/i. NHSSC names a framework after its clinical category, so the name is the key; the CBU category field is far too broad to filter on. COVERAGE LIMIT, STATED RATHER THAN HIDDEN. Total Orthopaedic Solutions 3 is the main NHS Supply Chain route for this patch and carries 101 named suppliers, but being named on it is evidence of a route, not of volume, and NHS Supply Chain is only one route. The award record below shows orthopaedic and trauma implants bought through NHS Wales Shared Services, National Procurement in Scotland, the Business Services Organisation in Northern Ireland and trusts' own direct awards, none of which appears in the framework list above. Surgical Navigation Systems is shared with neurosurgery and ENT. No unit or market-share split is published for any of it, and none is claimed here.",
  "suppliers": "Every supplier NHS Supply Chain names on the frameworks above, resolved to one name per company through the Hub's alias registry, and ordered by how many of this speciality's frameworks they appear on. That count is the only claim made. It is not a ranking of size or share. Where NHS Supply Chain spelled a company two ways across its own pages, both spellings are shown against the one entry. COVERAGE LIMIT, STATED RATHER THAN HIDDEN. Total Orthopaedic Solutions 3 is the main NHS Supply Chain route for this patch and carries 101 named suppliers, but being named on it is evidence of a route, not of volume, and NHS Supply Chain is only one route. The award record below shows orthopaedic and trauma implants bought through NHS Wales Shared Services, National Procurement in Scotland, the Business Services Organisation in Northern Ireland and trusts' own direct awards, none of which appears in the framework list above. Surgical Navigation Systems is shared with neurosurgery and ENT. No unit or market-share split is published for any of it, and none is claimed here.",
  "awards": "Award-stage notices whose TITLE matches /\\b(orthopaedic\\w*|orthopedic\\w*|orthobiologic\\w*|trauma\\w*|tos3|arthroplast\\w*|joint replacement|hip\\b|knee\\b|shoulder\\b|elbow\\b|ankle\\b|spinal|spine\\b|scoliosis|vertebr\\w*|pedicle|interbody|kyphoplast\\w*|vertebroplast\\w*|discectom\\w*|laminectom\\w*|fractur\\w*|osteotom\\w*|osteosynthes\\w*|femur|acetabul\\w*|bone (?:cement|graft|substitute|prep|screw|anchor|plate|mill|void filler)|arthroscop\\w*|cruciate|meniscal|meniscus|external fixation|fixator|intramedullary|tourniquet\\w*|sagittal saw|pulse lavage|musculoskelet\\w*|limb reconstruction)\\b/i and does not match /\\b(medicines|spinal cord stimulat\\w*|epidural|fgm|sexual abuse|spinal muscular atrophy)\\b/i. The exclusion list exists because every pattern in it matched a real notice that was not this speciality. A CPV code beginning 331417 or 33183 or 85121283 is recorded as corroboration where the feed carries one, but never admits a notice on its own: a notice carrying a basket of CPV codes is filed under all of them and bought under one. Buyer names are never matched on.",
  "openTenders": "Notices still open for bidding, matched the same way. An empty list means no open notice on this patch today, not that none was looked for.",
  "drugTariff": "No Drug Tariff part applies to this speciality. Part IX reimburses dressings and elastic hosiery (IXA), incontinence appliances (IXB), stoma appliances (IXC) and elastic hosiery (IXR); nothing on this patch is listed there, so the panel carries no tariff rather than reaching for the nearest part."
